  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PACT Promot. citizen engagement in Democratic Development in Cambodia, 2016-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PACT &#xD6;kat medborgligt deltagande i decentraliseringsprocess i Kambodja 2016-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROCEED II aims to contribute to the following project goal: &quot;Sub-national administrations are more accountable to diverse citizens&quot;. The programme has two main outcomes: - Diverse citizen groups more effectively voice their needs and feedback to influence sub-national administration decisions. - Sub-national administrations address more citizen issues. The results framework follows the theory of change presented by Pact and remains consistent with the approach of the previous programme phase, PROCEED I.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Pact Institute har till Sida ans&#xF6;kt om finansiering f&#xF6;r 15 miljoner kronor f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra projektet &quot;Promoting Citizen Engagement in Democratic Development, phase II (PROCEED II)&quot; i Kambodja under perioden februari 2016 - oktober 2018. PROCEED II &#xE4;r en forts&#xE4;ttning p&#xE5; ett tidigare fas genomf&#xF6;rd av Pact och med finansiering fr&#xE5;n Sida.

Projektets l&#xE5;ngsiktiga m&#xE5;l &#xE4;r att bidra till att lokala myndigheter blir mer ansvarstagande gentemot medborgarna. Direkt syftar projektet till att n&#xE5; tv&#xE5; delm&#xE5;l: 1) olika medborgargrupper f&#xF6;r mer effektivt fram sina behov och &#xE5;sikter gentemot sina lokala myndigheter 2) lokala myndigheter hanterar fler fr&#xE5;gor fr&#xE5;n medborgarna. Pact kommer att genomf&#xF6;ra projektet tillsammans med fem lokala organisationer i Kambodja som i sin tur st&#xF6;djer organisationer och individer p&#xE5; gr&#xE4;srotsniv&#xE5;. Geografiskt kommer projektet att genomf&#xF6;ras i fyra provinser och tolv distrikt. Pact kommer ocks&#xE5; att st&#xF6;dja ett n&#xE4;tverk p&#xE5; nationell niv&#xE5; i syfte att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra dialogen mellan det civila samh&#xE4;llet och den kambodjanska regeringen avseende landets decentraliseringsreform.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pact Institute has applied to Sida for funding of 15 million SEK to carry out the project &quot;Promoting Citizen Engagement in Democratic Development, phase II (PROCEED II)&quot; in Cambodia during the period February 2016 - October 2018. PROCEED II is a continuation of an earlier phase implemented by the Pact and with financing from Sida.

The intervention overall goal is to contribute to sub-national administrations to be more accountable to diverse citizens. In doing so, the project aims at reaching two main objectives: 1) diverse citizen groups more effectively voice their needs and feedback to influence sub-national administration decisions 2) sub-national administrations address more citizen issues. Pact will implement the project together with five local NGOs in Cambodia who in their turn support community based organisations, grass-root organisations and individuals across four provinces and twelve district/municipalities. Pact will also support one network on national level in order to improve the civil society dialogue with the government on the Cambodian decentralisation reform.</narrative>
  </description>
